  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Our grant proposal promised to 'uncover regulatory signatures' in kidney transplant biopsies, and now I have to turn that into an actual analysis. I have expression for 25 biopsies, a TF motif prior and a PPI file. Where do I go from here?"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Routing matched these registered workflows to your words, but the capability check did not confirm that any of them gives what you asked for:\n- **PANDA** — produces: One weighted TF-to-gene regulatory network across all the samples given.\n- **PUMA** — produces: One weighted network of how TFs and miRNAs regulate genes, across all samples.\n- **LIONESS-PANDA** — produces: One TF-gene network per sample, plus the aggregate network.\n- **LIONESS-PUMA** — produces: One TF/miRNA-gene network per sample, plus the aggregate network.\n- **OTTER** — produces: One weighted TF-to-gene regulatory network across all samples, fitted so that it agrees with the PPI network and gene co-expression.\n- **GIRAFFE** — produces: A signed TF-to-gene regulatory matrix (positive activating, negative repressing), across all samples. Each TF's activity in each sample, estimated apart from its own mRNA level.\n\nCompare what each produces with what you asked for. Ask again to re-run the check, or say which result you want and from which workflow.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
